Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
A Schrodinger-cat state and the negativity of its Wigner function\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A coherent state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 " is the most classical state a single mode of light can be in: its Wigner \
function is a Gaussian bump sitting at the point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 " that the classical amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " marks out, and it is non-negative everywhere, so it behaves like an \
ordinary probability density over phase space. A Schrodinger-cat state is the \
superposition of two such classical-like fields pulled far apart,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"|", "\[Psi]", "\[RightAngleBracket]", "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"|", "\[Alpha]"}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[Phi]"}]], "|", "-", "\[Alpha]", "\[RightAngleBracket]",
     ")", ","}],
   TraditionalForm],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with ",
 Cell[BoxData["\|01d4a9"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " fixing the norm and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " the relative phase. When ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " is large the two pieces are macroscopically distinguishable, which is the \
\"dead and alive\" picture Schrodinger used to needle the Copenhagen \
interpretation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["\<\
The question this example answers is what happens to the Wigner function in \
between the two lobes. The two coherent pieces are classical on their own, \
but their superposition is not, and phase space records the difference in one \
sharp way: the Wigner function develops oscillating fringes between the \
lobes, and those fringes dip below zero. A negative Wigner function has no \
classical probability interpretation, so it is the cleanest signature that \
the state is nonclassical. We build the state in the Wolfram QuantumFramework \
(QF), read its photon-number structure, compute the Wigner function, and \
watch the negativity appear exactly where the two branches interfere.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Throughout, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], "=", "{", "1", ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " is the vacuum and the Fock states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 " carry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " photons; we truncate the infinite ladder at a finite cutoff, which the \
last section checks."
}], "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell["Building the cat: a superposition of two coherent states", "Section",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Setting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " makes an ",
 StyleBox["even cat",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " an ",
 StyleBox["odd cat",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " the Yurke-Stoler state. Load the checked-out QF paclet:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"PacletDirectoryLoad", 
  "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework/\
QuantumFramework/\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["Load the main context:", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell["\<\
Expose the bosonic (second-quantization) context, which holds the Fock-space \
states and the phase-space functions:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"",
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bosonic states live on a truncated Fock space of size ",
 Cell[BoxData["$FockSize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 "; set a cutoff of 40 levels, comfortably above the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "\[TildeTilde]", "8"}]],
   "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " photons we will put in:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"SetFockSpaceSize", "[", "40", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CatState", "[", "size", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " builds the normalized superposition on a space of the given size; with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CatState", "[", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 " the size defaults to ",
 Cell[BoxData["$FockSize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 ". Build an even cat with a real amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "2.8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"even", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CatState", "[", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"2.8", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "And the odd cat, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"odd", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CatState", "[", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"2.8", ",", " ", "Pi"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both carry about eight photons and sit as two lobes on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 "-axis at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", 
   SqrtBox["2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 ", since a real ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " displaces along position only."
}], "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell["\<\
Even and odd photon numbers: the interference in the number basis\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The superposition is already visible before we reach phase space. Expanding \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " in Fock states, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 " amplitudes carry a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 ", so adding the two coherent states (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 ") cancels every odd ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " and doubles every even ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 ", while subtracting them (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ") does the reverse. Read the first ten photon-number probabilities of the \
even cat; ",
 Cell[BoxData["Chop"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " sets the tiny machine-precision residue to zero so the comb is readable:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"even", "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "10"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell["\<\
Only even photon numbers survive. Do the same for the odd cat:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"odd", "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", "10"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the two combs are interleaved: the even cat lives on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", "4"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " and the odd cat on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "5"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 ". That strict alternation is the interference between the two coherent \
branches, written in the photon-number basis. The same even-or-odd structure \
makes a cat an eigenstate of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 ": removing two photons maps even to even and odd to odd, and returns the \
same state. Build the annihilation operator:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Confirm that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " sends the even cat to a multiple of itself, by checking that the \
normalized result is the original state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"QuantumSimilarity", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", "[", "a", "]"}], "[", "even", "]"}], ")"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Normalize\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "even"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The similarity is one, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "\[Proportional]", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 ". Read off the eigenvalue as the expectation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"SuperDagger", "[", "even", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "@", " ", "even"}]}]}], ")"}], "[", "\"\<Scalar\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The eigenvalue is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 ": both coherent pieces ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " are eigenstates of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " with eigenvalues ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 ", so each is an eigenstate of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 " with the common eigenvalue ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 ", and so is any superposition of them."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell["\<\
The Wigner function: two lobes, fringes, and a dip below zero\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"WignerRepresentation", "[", 
   RowBox[{"state", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"xmin", ",", "xmax"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"ymin", ",", "ymax"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " returns the Wigner function as an ",
 Cell[BoxData["InterpolatingFunction"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],
 " over the requested window. Compute it for the even cat:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"wig", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"WignerRepresentation", "[", 
   RowBox[{"even", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell["Plot it over the phase plane:", "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot3D", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"wig", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<TemperatureMap\>\""}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotPoints", " ", "->", " ", "80"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mesh", " ", "->", " ", "15"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"MeshStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", ".2", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"AxesLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<p\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<W(x,p)\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"LabelStyle", " ", "->", " ", "13"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Wigner function of the even cat state (\[Alpha]=2.8)\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two Gaussian lobes sit at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", 
   SqrtBox["2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],
 ", the phase-space images of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 ". Between them runs a ridge of fringes that oscillate along ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 ", with no classical counterpart: they are the interference of the two \
branches. The smallest value on the grid is the deepest fringe:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{"wig", "[", "\"\<ValuesOnGrid\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is negative. Two separated Gaussians alone would make a non-negative \
function; the negativity is created entirely by the cross term between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 ", and it lives in the region between them, not on the lobes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell["The origin value and the photon-number parity", "Section",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The deepest and the highest points of the fringe pattern both sit at the \
origin, halfway between the lobes, and the value there is fixed by a \
symmetry. The Wigner function at the origin is proportional to the \
expectation of the photon-number parity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 ", which assigns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 " to even Fock states and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " to odd ones. The even cat has only even photons and the odd cat only odd \
ones, so each is an eigenstate of parity:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"DiagonalMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ")"}], "^", 
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"$FockSize", " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", ".",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
   " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"even", ",", " ", "odd"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The even cat is an even-parity eigenstate and the odd cat an odd-parity \
one, opposite eigenvalues of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 ", so their Wigner functions sit at opposite extremes of the origin value. \
Evaluate the even cat's representation at the origin:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"wig", "[", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 ", the largest value a Wigner function can take in this convention: ",
 Cell[BoxData["WignerRepresentation"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 " normalizes the vacuum to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "0"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 " and bounds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["W", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[LessEqual]", "1", "/", 
   "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 ", so a parity of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 " pins the even cat to the top of that range and a parity of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 " pins the odd cat to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A note on conventions, because QF offers a second route that scales \
differently. The closed-form point-value function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"WignerFunction", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", " ", "\[Alpha]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 " works in the complex amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " and normalizes the vacuum to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ". Its origin value for the even cat is:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"WignerFunction", "[", 
  RowBox[{"even", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "2", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 ", and the odd cat gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "2", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 ". The factor of two against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"wig", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " is just the Jacobian between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 "; the physics, parity times the vacuum peak, is the same in both."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell["\<\
The contrast with a classical state is immediate. Build the coherent state \
with the same amplitude:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"coh", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CoherentState", "[", "]"}], "[", "2.8", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell["Compute its Wigner function:", "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"wigCoh", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"WignerRepresentation", "[", 
   RowBox[{"coh", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell["Its smallest value on the grid is:", "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{"wigCoh", "[", "\"\<ValuesOnGrid\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell["\<\
Zero to machine precision: the coherent Wigner function is a single \
non-negative Gaussian, with none of the fringes. Placing the two side by side \
shows what the superposition adds:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"cf", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Blend", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"Blue", ",", " ", "White", ",", " ", "Red"}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"Rescale", "[", 
          RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "Pi"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "Pi"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
      ")"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"GraphicsRow", "[", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", "\n", "      ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"DensityPlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"#1", "[", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "p"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "5"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotPoints", " ", "->", " ", "120"}], ",", "\n", 
          "        ", 
          RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "cf"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"ColorFunctionScaling", " ", "->", " ", "False"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "Pi"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "Pi"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
          RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<p\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "#2"}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
          
          RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
           RowBox[{"BarLegend", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"cf", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "/", "Pi"}], ",", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"1", "/", "Pi"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"LegendLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<W\>\""}]}], 
            "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"wig", ",", " ", "wigCoh"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          
          RowBox[{"\"\<even cat: fringes dip below zero\>\"", ",", 
           " ", "\"\<coherent state: non-negative Gaussian\>\""}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"Spacings", " ", "->", " ", "20"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell["Checking the truncation", "Section",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Everything above lives on a Fock space cut at 40 levels. A cat with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "\[TildeTilde]", "8"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " photons has negligible population that high, but confirm it rather than \
assume it. The total weight above level 30 is:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"even", "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"31", " ", ";;"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is vanishingly small, so the truncation does not distort the state, the \
fringes, or the origin value; raising ",
 Cell[BoxData["$FockSize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " leaves them unchanged."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],

Cell["What the Wigner function shows", "Section",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Schrodinger-cat state is a superposition of two coherent fields, and that \
superposition leaves two marks. In the photon-number basis it is a strict \
even-or-odd comb, which makes the cat an eigenstate of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 " with eigenvalue ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ". In phase space it is a ridge of fringes between the two coherent lobes, \
and those fringes go negative. The negativity is not an artifact of the \
lobes, which are classical Gaussians on their own; it is the interference \
between them, and its value at the origin is locked to the photon-number \
parity, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " for the even cat and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1", "/", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " for the odd one. A coherent state of the same amplitude shows none of \
this: its Wigner function is a single non-negative Gaussian. The dip below \
zero is the phase-space fingerprint of the superposition, and it is the \
reason a cat state is a resource no classical field can supply."
}], "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"
]
